### Azure AI Search Simulator - Collection Filter Sample
### Demonstrates Collection(Edm.Int32) fields and OData collection-filter lambda
### syntax ("field/any(x: predicate)") over both string and int collections.
### Use with REST Client extension in VS Code or similar tools
### Base URL: https://localhost:7250 (HTTPS) or http://localhost:5250 (HTTP)

# Variables loaded from .env file (copy .env.example to .env in the workspace root)

# BASE_URL=https://localhost:7250
# API_VERSION=2024-07-01
# ADMIN_KEY=admin-key-12345
# QUERY_KEY=query-key-67890

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5250
@apiVersion = 2024-07-01
@adminKey = admin-key-12345
@queryKey = query-key-67890

# ============================================
# INDEX MANAGEMENT
# ============================================

### Create the index (hotels + roomNumbers: Collection(Edm.Int32))
POST {{baseUrl}}/indexes?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json
api-key: {{adminKey}}

{
  "name": "hotels-int-collection",
  "fields": [
    { "name": "hotelId", "type": "Edm.String", "key": true, "filterable": true },
    { "name": "hotelName", "type": "Edm.String", "searchable": true, "filterable": true, "sortable": true },
    { "name": "description", "type": "Edm.String", "searchable": true },
    { "name": "category", "type": "Edm.String", "searchable": false, "filterable": false, "facetable": true },
    { "name": "rating", "type": "Edm.Double", "filterable": true, "sortable": true },
    { "name": "parkingIncluded", "type": "Edm.Boolean", "filterable": true },
    { "name": "lastRenovationDate", "type": "Edm.DateTimeOffset", "filterable": true, "sortable": true },
    { "name": "tags", "type": "Collection(Edm.String)", "searchable": true, "filterable": true },
    { "name": "roomNumbers", "type": "Collection(Edm.Int32)", "filterable": true, "facetable": true }
  ]
}

### Get the index
GET {{baseUrl}}/indexes/hotels-int-collection?api-version={{apiVersion}}
api-key: {{adminKey}}


### Delete the index
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/indexes/hotels-int-collection?api-version={{apiVersion}}
api-key: {{adminKey}}

# ============================================
# DOCUMENT OPERATIONS (Push Model)
# ============================================

### Upload documents (each hotel has a list of available room numbers)
POST {{baseUrl}}/indexes/hotels-int-collection/docs/index?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json
api-key: {{adminKey}}

{
  "value": [
    {
      "@search.action": "upload",
      "hotelId": "1",
      "hotelName": "Grand Azure Hotel",
      "description": "A luxurious hotel in the heart of downtown with stunning views and world-class amenities.",
      "category": "Luxury",
      "rating": 4.8,
      "parkingIncluded": true,
      "lastRenovationDate": "2023-06-15T00:00:00Z",
      "tags": ["luxury", "spa", "pool", "wifi"],
      "roomNumbers": [101, 102, 205]
    },
    {
      "@search.action": "upload",
      "hotelId": "2",
      "hotelName": "Budget Inn Express",
      "description": "Affordable accommodation for business travelers with free breakfast and parking.",
      "category": "Budget",
      "rating": 3.5,
      "parkingIncluded": true,
      "lastRenovationDate": "2020-01-10T00:00:00Z",
      "tags": ["budget", "breakfast", "wifi"],
      "roomNumbers": [301, 302]
    }
  ]
}

# ============================================
# FILTER QUERIES
# ============================================

### baseline: no filter
POST {{baseUrl}}/indexes/hotels-int-collection/docs/search?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json
api-key: {{queryKey}}

{
  "search": "*",
  "facets": ["category"]
}

### existing scalar filter (known-good, for comparison)
POST {{baseUrl}}/indexes/hotels-int-collection/docs/search?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json
api-key: {{queryKey}}

{
  "search": "*",
  "filter": "lastRenovationDate gt 2020-01-11"
}

### any() filter over the string collection "tags" (should match hotel 1 only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/indexes/hotels-int-collection/docs/search?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json
api-key: {{queryKey}}

{
  "search": "*",
  "filter": "tags/any(t: t eq 'luxury')"
}

### any() filter over the int collection "roomNumbers" (should match hotel 1 only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/indexes/hotels-int-collection/docs/search?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json
api-key: {{queryKey}}

{
  "search": "*",
  "filter": "roomNumbers/any(c: c eq 101)"
}

### any() with a numeric range predicate (should match hotel 2 only: rooms 301, 302)
POST {{baseUrl}}/indexes/hotels-int-collection/docs/search?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json
api-key: {{queryKey}}

{
  "search": "*",
  "filter": "roomNumbers/any(c: c gt 300)"
}

### any() with nested search.in() over the string collection (should match both hotels)
POST {{baseUrl}}/indexes/hotels-int-collection/docs/search?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json
api-key: {{queryKey}}

{
  "search": "*",
  "filter": "tags/any(t: search.in(t, 'spa,breakfast', ','))"
}

### all() is recognized but not supported - returns zero documents rather than
### silently matching every document. See docs/LIMITATIONS.md.
POST {{baseUrl}}/indexes/hotels-int-collection/docs/search?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json
api-key: {{queryKey}}

{
  "search": "*",
  "filter": "roomNumbers/all(c: c eq 101)"
}
